WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Open hardware you can verify: board design files from 29 hardware ecosystems, checked from the bytes, mirrored with their licences.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:10.300
322 development boards, one record each. Every format is true, false or unknown, and true needs bytes that were retrieved.

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:16.200
583 openly licensed CAD files from 232 boards, in the repository: Eagle, KiCad, Altium, Gerber, drill, STEP, STL and DXF. 0 problems in mirror.py check.

4
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.600
KiCad PCB: SparkFun IoT RedBoard RP2350, rendered from the vendor's file. CC BY-SA 4.0.

5
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.500
KiCad schematic: SparkFun Thing Plus ESP32-S3. CC BY-SA 4.0.

6
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.400
Eagle board files drawn layer by layer: Adafruit Feather RP2040 and SparkFun RedBoard Turbo. CC BY-SA.

7
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.300
Gerber fabrication set: SparkFun Edge, ten layers, top and bottom. CC BY-SA 4.0.

8
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.700
STEP model: BeagleBone AI-64, 163,393 triangles. CC BY 4.0.

9
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.100
STEP model: M5Stack Stamp-S3, tessellated with OpenCASCADE. MIT.

10
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.500
25 boards with a verified 3D model: PocketBeagle, BeagleBone AI-64, BeagleBone AI, Artemis, Pico Vision, Stamp-S3.

11
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:57.900
Our own designs, checked by simulation: a robotic joint in MuJoCo, a 48 V servo supply in ngspice, a UART in Icarus Verilog.

12
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:02.300
Licences travel with the files: an ATTRIBUTION.md for every board, a source link and digest for every file.

13
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:08.800
Use it in a course, a lab or a product. Universities: course labs, research, student projects. Companies: reference designs, joint grant proposals.
